<description>&lt;p&gt;Violence continues across South Sudan with armed groups ambushing civilians, killing two people in Jebel Boma County and five in a road ambush in Warrap County, while a truckload of alcohol was seized in Mundri West as part of a substance-abuse crackdown. A Christian woman was killed after refusing a forced marriage to a Muslim man and two pastors were wounded in a separate attack, prompting women in Greater Mundri to call for protection and accountability. The Western Equatoria governor barred personal bodyguards at SPLM congresses and the governor of Jonglei reported efforts to end clashes in Bor, Duk and Twic East, while elections were postponed again to February 2027. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxNUzVVZlh0cUIxWFBYU2NGYnZWdHZmc1RLY3oyNm51NTlQQjJEMFlVclNsN2tWM0FjMmRycVdsMXQ2WW4xeUJZYVR1V3lac2ZBTmJ4RWcxYXVxaFlGV1dNbXM3OG5FOXhheVdiM0dzUVktZnJZZkQxNUU4ZWZuM0lWV2JyZXVKUXZtcDl2RHVaTVRtRGN1ZFdPckdPQ0dZSFI1SDVfVGlPbWhYa0o0alNCNFdsSDgtUkhxakRWZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxPT2FRa1pCeDZMbTZNUV9TRl9wdFl2OFRWZGhXQXZyYkVxYVNnYkl6US02bHNrUG9NYXRtZHFURUJvMld2aVA1LXlBQmNKd2pFeWx6NDZ2LUROY0w1RDVfQUZsOWo3bW9WaFdtSXl5WlFXQ2Zlc3lWWERGNW1wSGRhSkp2RGxPWDNJUTdKcHBVeGlCcDZ0X1Vn?oc=5&quot;&gt;FTL Somalia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Billy Graham Evangelistic Association&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxOdmZINEdDem1zSlh5RGpjdmZnOFAzb01qX2M1Y1gtSEM0T3F2TlQ5ZE1xbmJvZG1sLWxxdmU4WXVlREtrcEw3cGpMcFpqWmo1Tkg2Rk14ZklvUE9IWE5ZRFgtQjg1bVhJelNqNXJvZXU2LWxpRU5ZNTVMWUhFSHVFM2V5cnNJX0pPbjhuWnhKYlFJWjNsUllTUkttbEpyQUpa?oc=5&quot;&gt;Christian News Network&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;h